From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:56:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] create a YUV buffer over R8 whatever it is used for

Whether the driver creates a resource in the buffer's own format or as the
bytes of an R8 image is decided by asking the host for the capabilities the
use flags name: render for rendering, sampler for texturing, scanout for
scanout. A buffer that no GPU unit uses (software access, a video decoder or
encoder, a camera) names none, so the answer is yes for every format, and
the driver asks the host to create an NV12 resource.

A host without an allocator cannot. The renderer has no storage for a
multi-planar format, refuses the request with an invalid parameter, and
answers the attach, the context attach, the transfer and the unref that
follow for that resource with an invalid resource id: six error replies and
a kernel log line each for every buffer, at the rate the codec allocates
them. The buffer itself is guest memory and keeps working, which is why
nothing else notices. The same buffer with a texture flag takes the R8
emulation, so the driver already handles the format; it only chose by use
flag instead of by what the host can create.

The blob decision made the same choice for a buffer the GPU samples without
the CPU, such as a decoder output: it asked the renderer for a blob of the
format itself, and the renderer failed the command with a context error.

Create, invalidate, flush and the blob decision now ask whether the
emulation carries the format whenever it can serve the request. A host that
has an allocator, one that advertises no capabilities and gfxstream are
untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 virtgpu_virgl.c | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/virtgpu_virgl.c b/virtgpu_virgl.c
index c99db486d39185640c82187fac7ed76c3a2c2865..5300be66af74fd834fd411f3302036ee4306b783 100644
--- a/virtgpu_virgl.c
+++ b/virtgpu_virgl.c
@@ -383,6 +383,29 @@ static bool virgl_supports_combination_through_emulation(struct driver *drv, uin
 	       drm_format == DRM_FORMAT_YVU420 || drm_format == DRM_FORMAT_YVU420_ANDROID;
 }
 
+// Whether this buffer exists only as the bytes of an R8 image. The native test above only checks
+// the capabilities the use flags name, so it answers yes for every format when no GPU unit uses the
+// buffer (software access, a video codec or a camera). A host without an allocator still has to
+// create a resource for such a buffer, and cannot create a multi-planar format at all: the renderer
+// answers the request with an invalid parameter, and every later command on the resource with an
+// invalid resource id. Whatever the buffer is used for, the emulation is the only way to have one.
+static bool virgl_is_emulated(struct driver *drv, uint32_t drm_format, uint64_t use_flags)
+{
+	struct virgl_priv *priv = (struct virgl_priv *)drv->priv;
+
+	// A host that advertises no capabilities (and gfxstream, which keeps its own) is not
+	// asked: it never refused a format here.
+	return priv->caps.max_version > 0 &&
+	       virgl_supports_combination_through_emulation(drv, drm_format, use_flags);
+}
+
+// Whether a resource for this buffer is created in the buffer's own format.
+static bool virgl_creates_natively(struct driver *drv, uint32_t drm_format, uint64_t use_flags)
+{
+	return !virgl_is_emulated(drv, drm_format, use_flags) &&
+	       virgl_supports_combination_natively(drv, drm_format, use_flags);
+}
+
 // Adds the given buffer combination to the list of supported buffer combinations if the
 // combination is supported by the virtio backend.
 static void virgl_add_combination(struct driver *drv, uint32_t drm_format,
@@ -516,7 +539,7 @@ static int virgl_3d_bo_create(struct bo *bo, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, ui
 	struct drm_virtgpu_resource_create res_create = { 0 };
 	struct bo_metadata emulated_metadata = { 0 };
 
-	if (virgl_supports_combination_natively(bo->drv, format, use_flags)) {
+	if (virgl_creates_natively(bo->drv, format, use_flags)) {
 		stride = drv_stride_from_format(format, width, 0);
 		drv_bo_from_format(bo, stride, 1, height, format);
 	} else {
@@ -977,6 +1000,11 @@ static bool should_use_blob(struct driver *drv, uint32_t format, uint64_t use_fl
 {
 	struct virgl_priv *priv = (struct virgl_priv *)drv->priv;
 
+	// The bytes of an R8 image are not described by a blob: the renderer would be asked
+	// for the format itself.
+	if (virgl_is_emulated(drv, format, use_flags))
+		return false;
+
 	/*
 	 * Only a blob resource carries a handle the renderer can hand to a
 	 * second context, so a buffer the GPU shares has to be one: the Vulkan
@@ -1165,7 +1193,7 @@ static int virgl_bo_invalidate(struct bo *bo, struct mapping *mapping)
 			xfer.level = bo->meta.strides[0];
 	}
 
-	if (virgl_supports_combination_natively(bo->drv, bo->meta.format, bo->meta.use_flags)) {
+	if (virgl_creates_natively(bo->drv, bo->meta.format, bo->meta.use_flags)) {
 		xfer_params.xfers_needed = 1;
 		xfer_params.xfer_boxes[0] = mapping->rect;
 	} else {
@@ -1241,7 +1269,7 @@ static int virgl_bo_flush(struct bo *bo, struct mapping *mapping)
 	if (priv->host_gbm_enabled)
 		xfer.level = bo->meta.strides[0];
 
-	if (virgl_supports_combination_natively(bo->drv, bo->meta.format, bo->meta.use_flags)) {
+	if (virgl_creates_natively(bo->drv, bo->meta.format, bo->meta.use_flags)) {
 		xfer_params.xfers_needed = 1;
 		xfer_params.xfer_boxes[0] = mapping->rect;
 	} else {
